    {
      "name": "Pseudostratified ciliated epithelium",
      "group": "Epithelium",
      "color": "#d9aac0",
      "description": "Respiratory epithelium – pseudostratified ciliated columnar epithelium with goblet cells. Every cell rests on the basement membrane but only ciliated and goblet cells reach the lumen, so nuclei lie at different levels and the single layer looks stratified. Also contains brush cells and neuroendocrine (Kulchitsky) cells. Chronic irritation (smoking) converts it to stratified squamous epithelium (squamous metaplasia). Existing sparse macro samples remain outside the registered cellular window; use the local field for cellular relationships.",
